# Names only — never values. The publisher reads these from the environment.
#
# On the host they live in ~/.config/biohack-gateway/publish/env, beside the access-key CSV that
# BIOHACK_ACCESS_KEYS_CSV points at. That directory is the publisher's; the gateway's systemd unit
# excludes it, so the service can read neither this file nor the key.
#
#   set -a; . ~/.config/biohack-gateway/publish/env; set +a
#
# The secret itself is not here: it is the console's access-key CSV, because the environment leaks
# (`/proc/<pid>/environ`, crash dumps, children) and a file the publisher reads does not.
#
# How to create the credential itself: deploy/README.md §5.
BIOHACK_BUCKET=
AWS_REGION=
BIOHACK_ACCESS_KEYS_CSV=
